[1] These are the priests and Levites who came up with Zerubbabel son of Shaltiel, and Jeshua: Seraiyah, Jeremiah, Ezra,
[2] Amariah, Maluch,
[3] Shecaniah,
[4] Edio, Gintoi, Abiyah,
[5] Miyamin, Maadyah, Bilgah,
[6] Shemaiyahu, Yoivar, Yedaiah,
[7] Salu, Amoq, Chilkiah, Yedaiah—these were the heads of the priests and their brothers in the days of Jeshua.
[8] And the Levites: Jeshua, Buni, Kadmiyel, Sherevyyah, Yehuda, Mattanyah—over the hands, he and his brothers, for the services.
[9] And Bakbukiyyah, and Oni, their brothers, opposite them for the watches.
[10] And Jeshua fathered Yoakim, and Yoakim fathered Eliashiv, and Eliashiv fathered Yoada,
[11] and Yoada fathered Yonatan, and Yonatan fathered Yadua.
[12] And in the days of Yoakim, his brothers the priests and the heads of the fathers were: to Seraiyah, Meraiyah; to Jeremiah, Chananyahu;
[13] to Ezra, Meshulam; to Amariyah, Yehoyanan;
[14] to Melicu, Yonatan; to Shebanyah, Yosef;
[15] to Charim, Adna; to Meraiyoth, Chelkai;
[16] to Edio, Zakaryah; to Gintoi, Meshulam;
[17] to Abiyah, Zikri; to Minyam, Bilgah; to Mo'adyah, Philtai;
[18] to Bilgah, Shammua; to Shemaiyahu, Yehonatan;
[19] and to Yoivar, Mattanya; to Yoada, Uzi;
[20] to Salai, Kalai; to Amoq, Eber;
[21] to Chilkiah, Chasavyah; to Yoada, Natanai;
[22] the Levites in the days of Eliashiv, Yoada, and Yochanan, and Yadua were written as heads of the fathers, and the priests in the kingdom of Darius the Persian.
[23] Sons of Levi, heads of the fathers, were written in the book of the days, until the days of Yochanan son of Eliashiv.
[24] And the heads of the Levites: Chasavyah, Sherevyyah, and Jeshua son of Kadmiyel, and their brothers opposite them to sing and to praise, by the command of David, the man of God, shift to shift.
[25] Mattanyah, Bakbukiyyah, Ovadyah, Meshulam, Talmon, and Akuv were gatekeepers, keeping the watches at the gates.
[26] These were in the days of Yoakim son of Jeshua, son of Yotsadak, and in the days of Nehemiah and Ezra the priest the scribe.
[27] And at the dedication of the wall of Jerusalem they sought the Levites from all their places to bring them to Jerusalem, to do the dedication and joy, with thanksgiving and with songs, with cymbals, with lyres and harps.
[28] And the sons of the singers were gathered, and from the plain around Jerusalem, and from the villages of Netophathi;
[29] from the house of Gilgal, and from the fields of Geba and Azmavet, for the Levites had built for themselves courts around Jerusalem.
[30] And the priests and Levites purified themselves, and they purified the people and the gates and the wall.
[31] And I brought up the leaders of Judah from above the wall, and I set two great thanksgivings and processions, one to the right above the wall toward the Ashpot Gate;
[32] and after them went Hosha'yah and half the leaders of Judah;
[33] and Azaryah, Ezra, and Meshulam;
[34] Yehuda and Binyamin and Shemaiyahu and Yirmiyah;
[35] and from the sons of the priests, in the trumpets: Zakaryah son of Yonatan, son of Shemaiyahu, son of Mattanyah, son of Meichaiyah, son of Zakur, son of Asaf;
[36] and his brothers Shemaiyahu and Azaryel, in the songs of the Levites, and Me'aly, Natanai, Yehuda, Chanani, with the instruments of song of David, the man of God, and Ezra the scribe before them.
[37] And above the Gate of the Singers, opposite them, we ascended to the steps of the city of David, on the ascent of the wall, from above the house of David to the Water Gate eastward;
[38] and the second thanksgiving procession went to the Molad, and I was behind it, and half the people on the wall, from above the Furnace Tower to the Broad Wall;
[39] and from above the Ephraim Gate, and on the Old Gate, and on the Fish Gate, and the Tower of Hananeel, and the Tower of the Hundred, to the Sheep Gate, and we stood at the Gate of the Fountain.
[40] And the two thanksgivings stood at the house of God, and I and half the officers with me.
[41] The priests: Eliyakim, Me'aseyah, Minyam, Meichaiyah, El'yoeinai, Zakaryah, Chanani, with the trumpets;
[42] and Me'aseyah, Shemaiyahu, El'azar, Uzi, Yehoyanan, Malkiyah, Eilam, Azar. And the singers made the sound, and Yizrachyahu the officer.
[43] And they offered great sacrifices that day, and they rejoiced, for the Lord had rejoiced them with great joy, and also the women and the children rejoiced, and the joy of Jerusalem was heard from afar.
[44] And they appointed men on that day over the levies, for the storehouses, the tithes, the first fruits and the contributions, to collect them for the cities' officers, for the portions to the priests and Levites, for the joy of Judah was on the priests and on the Levites who stood.
[45] And they kept the watch of their God, and the watch of the cleansing, and the singers and the gatekeepers, as the command of David and his son Solomon.
[46] For in the days of David and Asaph from the beginning, the heads of the singers and the song of praise and thanksgiving to God.
[47] And all Israel in the days of Zerubbabel and in the days of Nehemiah gave portions to the singers and the gatekeepers, a daily portion each day, and they consecrated the Levites, and the Levites consecrated the sons of Aaron.

---
Notes
- v. 25: "Mattanyah, Bakbukiyyah, Ovadyah, Meshulam, Talmon, and Akuv were gatekeepers, keeping the watches at the gates" — the Hebrew lists them as gatekeepers with their roles, and the structure is clearly a list of names followed by their shared role.
- v. 35–36: The genealogy of Zakaryah and his brothers' involvement in the songs is presented as a continuation, not as separate clauses, so the translation is structured accordingly.
- v. 47: "a daily portion each day" — the Hebrew uses a double expression of daily to emphasize the regularity, hence the repetition in English.
